{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/46108-status-social-skills-and-disciplines","id":46108,"title":"Status, Social Skills and Disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-09T23:50:56-08:00","id":46108,"title":"Status, Social Skills and Disciplines","content":"So, the Status merit, as we know, adds dice to the social rolls of characters when working to influence others who share that same group affiliation. I'm a little unclear on how -far- that effect extends, though.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming that various status types can stack; let's say the Prince of a city has 5 in City status, 5 in clan status (ventrue), and 5 in covenant status (invictus). When dealing with an underling in the same city, clan and covenant, I'm assuming this would mean he'd have a +15 to his dice pool (and a +10 or +5 if dealing with non-ventrue and/or non-invictus). Is this correct or would that be over-reaching?<br /> <br /> That aside, what about adding the dice to, say, social disciplines like Dominate or Majesty (or Nightmare, maybe)? Will your influence carry that same weight when applied to supernatural commands? How about the Predatory Aura conflicts; would the status bonuses add in there too? On one hand, I can imagine the same Invictus Ventrue prince as above being an unholy terror, dropping the full weight of his power, prestige, and position upon those who displease him. On the other hand, I wonder if it's something that's mechanically 'allowed'.<br /> <br /> As a final aside, the Invictus merit &quot;Notary&quot; has an added bonus in that no other Invictus can use their status in social rolls against you, since you're supposed to be a powerful, but 'neutral' arbiter and recorder of Oaths. The rules also suggest avoiding using pure dice in situations between NPCs and Players when the NPC is attempting social actions\u2014it should be a purely role-played thing ... unless, perhaps, disciplines or Predatory Aura come into play. The way it's worded makes me wonder, then, if those status points can otherwise be applied to those who <i>don't </i>have this sort of exception as the merit grants.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T23:57:28-08:00","id":46115,"title":"","content":"Status is just a relationship thing between the vampires. I would not allow status to improve supernatural capabilities (disciplines, lashing out), just because an elder outside shouldn't be weaker than an ancilae with status 3. Supernatural power should only come from the person himself, not from the cities opinion about him. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T00:00:51-08:00","id":46117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/46108-status-social-skills-and-disciplines?p=46115#post46115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Status is just a relationship thing between the vampires. I would not allow status to improve supernatural capabilities (disciplines, lashing out), just because an elder outside shouldn't be weaker than an ancilae with status 3. Supernatural power should only come from the person himself, not from the cities opinion about him.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a joke to be made about Carthian Law in here somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T00:06:44-08:00","id":46119,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but it's really a different case all together. It's part of Carthian Law, and it's pretty much the only magical power that i've know which comes purely from the beliefs of the masses. So I think Carthian Law is just an exception to the rule. (Or it will be in my game..)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T00:18:11-08:00","id":46126,"title":"","content":"That's what I do wonder, too; I'm just somewhat confused by the contradictory statement of the Notary merit. It seems to suggest that the status bonus could be used otherwise, when normally NPCs don't 'get to' manipulate players just based on social skills dice rolls. Maybe the feat itself is just poorly worded in that regard compared to the main social conflicts conceit (since players don't have doors and resolve, even if their characters do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T06:17:10-08:00","id":46204,"title":"","content":"Well I think that just because one merit has a strange wording it does not support assuming that the whole system supports this.<br /> After all, if this were true, City Status merit would definitely note it, because this would be huge, giving elders even a greater advantage against neonates (+3-5 dice on disciplines.. ouch..)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T09:30:30-08:00","id":46310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/46108-status-social-skills-and-disciplines?p=46126#post46126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I do wonder, too; I'm just somewhat confused by the contradictory statement of the Notary merit. It seems to suggest that the status bonus could be used otherwise, when normally NPCs don't 'get to' manipulate players just based on social skills dice rolls. Maybe the feat itself is just poorly worded in that regard compared to the main social conflicts conceit (since players don't have doors and resolve, even if their characters do).</div> </div> </div> </div> NPCs are not the only characters capable of using social actions. Presumably this Merit protects PCs against social interactions of other PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T09:41:47-08:00","id":46319,"title":"","content":"Also, the whole rule about &quot;having your last door opened choose whenever to do the action or take a different condition&quot; is there to also allow NPCs to actually use social manoeuvring against PCs. With this, social stats of NPCs actually matter, and that 5 presence 5 manipulation 5 socialise striking looks daeva can actually convince PCs of stuff, and they can't just fully ignore her looks and friendliness and decide that they hate her","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T10:00:32-08:00","id":46328,"title":"","content":"Also not all social actions will boil down to the social maneuvering mechanics. You can still resolve some situations with straight opposed rolls. An NPC notary would, btw, be immune to Status (Invictus) of the PC (and vice versa). Then there is the social combat system from Invite Only/Danse Macabre that can still be used. It also would be affected by the Notary merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T18:15:44-08:00","id":46639,"title":"","content":"Isn't this what Conditions are all about? They're a way to put mental and social strains on players while escaping the age-old 'trap' of mind controlling/taking control away from the players. Social rolls by NPC should put Conditions on the player, and then it's up to them if they go with it (gaining beats) or decide not to play along (no beats).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T19:52:52-08:00","id":47818,"title":"","content":"Murder of Crows does bring up a good point for me; I had also realized lately that, while a slightly asymmetrical example, if both an NPC and a PC were attempting to sway a third party, that might also be a way in which status might be rendered invalid by the Notary merit or other similar advantages. Taking it further, I don't know if it would be applicable to, say, the Debate rules from <i>Requiem for Rome</i>, but it's food for thought at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T14:14:13-07:00","id":709272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/46108-status-social-skills-and-disciplines?p=46117#post46117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a joke to be made about Carthian Law in here somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's called the Mandate of the Masses merit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}